id: pm-ado-toolchain-1104
title: Migrate pm-toolchain PR 87 to the November 4 SDK contract
description: "Update the grouped toolchain in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/87, reproduce failures, classify SDK contract changes, and preserve coverage and rollback checks."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-ado#87",migration,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-04T18:56:17.383Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T20:15:28.547Z"
author: codex-toolchain-1104
acceptance_criteria: Exact requested toolchain pins; meaningful contract assertions; passing package tests and all four unchanged coverage thresholds; typecheck and generated output current; evidence and remaining risks recorded.
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T18:56:21.320Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Plan: synchronized origin/main and confirmed registry latest versions pm-cli 2026.11.4, pm-ops 2026.11.4, pm-changelog 2026.10.31. Reproduce focused failures before changing assertions, then run the full suite and unchanged coverage gate serially."
  "2026-11-04T18:57:09.462Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (coupling): test/sdk-adoption.test.ts required docs to echo the exact development pin (main 2026.10.28 versus PR 2026.11.1/new 2026.11.4), so every bump broke it independently of runtime behavior. Replace that assertion with docs matching the declared peer/manifest minimum 2026.10.23; retain separate 2026.10.27 managed-preview capability requirement. Focused baseline: 1 passed, 1 failed."
  "2026-11-04T18:58:36.801Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Root cause (production): pm-cli 2026.10.30 GH-1614 preserves typed sentinel data. normalizeAssigneeValue and the SDK-free discovery projection instead erased none/null identities, corrupting semantic comparison and Azure export. Removed sentinel interpretation; empty input still follows explicit unset. Existing SDK oracle failed on none, and the new typed-sentinel regression failed against the original implementation (0/1) before the fix. Updated the exact expected normalized null identity and documentation."
  "2026-11-04T19:01:12.946Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Focused corrected files passed 40/40 tests (contracts, normalization, SDK adoption). Linked pm test rerun passed 9/9; typecheck and docstring gate passed (19 files, 128 declarations). Changelog regenerated after fetching tags; check passes with no changelog drift. No lint script is declared. Only package.json and package-lock.json pin the development toolchain; declared compatibility minimums and historical receipts remain intentional."
  "2026-11-04T19:11:40.942Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Additional gates passed: native precondition matrix 19/19; production audit found zero vulnerabilities; local pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exited 0. Full npm test remains in progress through packed project/global runtime acceptance. Author audit retains original Dependabot history; every newly authored commit is checked separately against the exact required SteveBot identity without rewriting history."
  "2026-11-04T19:16:03.641Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Full-suite follow-up: correcting the assignee documentation also changes the generated normalization.d.ts docstring. The exact current declaration snapshot gate correctly detected that comment drift. Reproduced test/public-api.test.ts separately, reviewed the one-line documentation-only declaration diff, and ran the documented current snapshot updater. No exported signatures or immutable published declarations/consumer fixtures changed. This is a generated-artifact consequence of the GH-1614 production fix, not a weakened API assertion."
  "2026-11-04T19:16:41.376Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Current public-API snapshot and unchanged published consumer now pass 2/2. Explicitly reverted only normalization.ts to origin/main, ran the new typed-sentinel regression and confirmed the expected 0/1 failure, then restored the fix before any final suite. The initial npm test run was stopped after finding the now-corrected snapshot drift; it is not claimed passing. Running the CI coverage command serially as the final complete-suite gate, with the unchanged 100% thresholds."
  "2026-11-04T19:53:47.354Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Focused packed-install recheck under CI Node 26.13.0 with V8 test instrumentation passes 12/12 (eleven launcher/global-runtime cases plus parent), zero failed/canceled/skipped, in about 14 minutes. No timeout, workload, worker, assertion or coverage-threshold changes. This is artifact/installer acceptance, not authored-source coverage: the focused report has no matching authored source files. The full package coverage attempt remains active with one earlier setup failure; do not infer all four coverage dimensions from the focused run."
  "2026-11-04T19:53:49.649Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Pin audit: package.json and package-lock.json hold the exact current development toolchain. test/packed-install-shapes.test.ts deliberately retains the 2026.10.25 compatibility host and the below-2026.10.27 preview refusal checks; bumping that fixture to the development SDK would remove older-host coverage. Documentation now uses the declared 2026.10.23 minimum and separate feature-specific host requirements instead of a volatile development pin."
  "2026-11-04T20:05:57.640Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Documentation also distinguishes SDK 2026.11.4 expected-item-hash guards (GH-1576, now released) from this package existing history fence and remaining write window. No new cross-process isolation or monotonic-history guarantee is claimed, and adopting additional guarded writes is outside this dependency migration. The exact minimum-docs assertion remains in place."
  "2026-11-04T20:08:53.825Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Bounded final coverage attempt: 807 reported tests, 805 passed and 2 failed. One failure is the compatibility-fixture npm global install being killed with empty output under its existing 180-second command deadline; the independent Node 26 V8-instrumented packed matrix passed 12/12 unchanged. The other is the sync worker deliberately stopped near the 75-minute repository budget during the long seeded model. Partial V8 totals are lines 78.81%, branches 98.83%, functions 83.24%; statements did not run. These are incomplete measurements, not a passing coverage gate. No threshold, ignore, assertion or timeout was changed. Remaining full-gate verification is pending; the existing pm-ado-packed-timeout follow-up records related load-sensitive fixture timing."
  "2026-11-04T20:08:56.161Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Final verified checks: focused contract/normalization/docs files 40/40; current snapshot plus unchanged published consumer 2/2; latest docs rerun 2/2; linked normalization/docs test 9/9; native precondition matrix 19/19; Node 26 packed matrix 12/12. Typecheck, docstrings (19 files/128 declarations), strict pm health, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), and regenerated changelog check pass. No lint script exists. Root production fix is 10b21fc; reviewed current declaration snapshot is 70c4619. Releasing the claim while retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-04T20:15:26.000Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Dependabot refreshed its remote head during verification, so the first push was rejected without changing the PR. Merged that refreshed head, retained the main package/manifest version 2026.11.4, rebuilt the lock from main with the exact requested toolchain pins, and reran npm ci, build, typecheck and 11 normalization/docs/public-consumer tests: all pass. Regenerated changelog/check after tag refresh also pass. The earlier bounded full-coverage receipt predates this release-version refresh and remains incomplete; no full-gate approval is claimed."
